<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37478" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praecursĭo</span></b> ,
		ōnis, f.
		id., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				coming</i> or <i>going before.</i>
			*</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sine praecursione visorum,</span>”
				<i>without a previous occurrence of phenomena</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Fat. 19, 44</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			partic. *</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> In
			milit. lang., <i>a preliminary combat</i>, <i>a skirmish</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep.
				6, 13, 6</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In rhet. lang., <i>a preparation</i> of the
			hearer, <i><span class="en">Cic. Top. 15,
			59</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>C.</b>
			<i>The office</i> or <i>work of a
				forerunner</i>, <i>the mission of John the
			Baptist</i>, <i><span class="en">Aug. Tract. in Johan. 4, 6</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Latin Dictionary</u>
        </u> (Charlton T. Lewis, Charles Short, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1879) </div>
</div>